.TH IMG349CTL 1 "October 2026" "img349ctl 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
img349ctl \- configure the Inca IMG\-349 gaming mouse
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B img349ctl
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B img349ctl
configures the Inca IMG\-349 gaming mouse (USB ID 1bcf:08b8) without the vendor's
Windows software: DPI levels and colours, LED mode, button bindings and polling rate.
.PP
The mouse keeps its settings in its own memory and can report them, so there is no
profile file. All button functions, including media keys and shortcuts, are carried
out by the mouse itself; no background program is needed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-device " PATH"
Use this hidraw node instead of detecting the mouse.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the reports instead of sending them.
.SH COMMANDS
Commands that change a setting write only what differs and read it back to check.
.TP
.B status
Show the detected mouse and its settings.
.TP
.B actions
List what buttons can be bound to.
.TP
.BI backup " FILE"
Save the mouse's whole memory to a file. Nothing can restore such a file; it is for
reference.
.TP
.BI dpi " LEVEL VALUE"
Set a level (1\-6) to 200, 400, 600, 800, 1000, 1200, 1600, 2000, 2400, 3200, 4800 or 6400.
.TP
.BI level " LEVEL"
Switch to a DPI level.
.TP
.BI color " LEVEL COLOUR"
Set a level's LED colour. LEVEL can be
.BR all ,
COLOUR is RRGGBB or a name such as red, orange or cyan.
.TP
.BI single " COLOUR"
One colour at every DPI level: DPI colour mode with every level set to COLOUR.
The light keeps breathing; the mouse has no steady mode.
.TP
.BR led " [" \fIMODE\fR "] [" \-\-speed " " \fIN\fR "] [" \-\-half | \-\-full ]
LED mode (dpi, colorful, rainbow, floe, waltz, seasons, off), speed (0 is fastest,
7 slowest) and brightness.
.TP
.BI rate " HZ"
Polling rate: 125, 250, 500 or 1000. The mouse disconnects for a moment and restarts.
.TP
.BI button " BUTTON ACTION " "[\-\-mode a|b]"
Bind a button (1\-7). The left button of mode A cannot be changed.
.TP
.BR mode " a|b"
Choose the mode in use.
.TP
.B reset
Put the settings back to the values read from a new mouse.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70\-img349\-mouse.rules
Gives the logged\-in user access to the mouse (from the source tree:
.IR contrib/70\-img349\-mouse.rules ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
img349ctl dpi 1 800              # first level: 800 DPI
img349ctl color all red          # every level red
img349ctl led dpi \-\-speed 2       # show the DPI colour
img349ctl button 4 volume\-up     # side button raises the volume
img349ctl button 5 keys:ctrl+c   # side button copies
img349ctl \-n reset               # show what a reset would send
.fi
.SH BUGS
Macros and the fire function's repeat count and interval are not supported. See
https://github.com/EmreYavuzalp/Inca\-IMG349\-Linux/issues
